{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Benefits of Object Oriented Programming "}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when talking about benefits of OOP"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Build the macrosystem conceptual model following the customer requirements, through the use and interpretation of collected information, represented in class diagrams, interaction diagrams, and operation contracts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Demonstrative pronouns in affirmative statements and questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">demonstrative pronouns</span> to point or identify specific things within a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>You use <strong><i>This, That, These</i></strong> and<i> <strong>Those</strong></i> as demonstrative pronouns&nbsp;</p> <p>You use demonstrative pronouns before nouns in a sentence.</p> <p>You use <strong><i>This </i></strong>and<strong><i> These</i></strong> to point nearby things.</p> <p>You use <strong><i>That </i></strong>and<strong><i> Those</i></strong> to point far things.</p> <p>You can use <strong>demonstrative pronouns</strong> in affirmative sentences or interrogative sentences. To use <strong>demonstrative pronouns</strong> within interrogative sentences, you need to use a regular grammar structure for questions and add the demonstrative pronoun right before the noun.</p></i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Demonstratives with Singular Nouns "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This / That\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Noun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"software\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"is\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"empty\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"That\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Program\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Is\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"new\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do those benefits include things like good reusability?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, the benefits are better maintainability, this means that the software can be more comprehensible and less fragile."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you know any of these ideas?"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Is this software empty?  &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;               -   &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;     Is that program new?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Demonstratives with Plural Nouns"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"These / Those\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Noun\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"These\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"principles\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"important.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Those\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"programs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"new.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Are these principles important?   &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;    -   &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Are those programs new?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That is why, we need to create classes by object-oriented modeling the real world, so it can be easily understood."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs with infinitives, need to, in affirmative statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">verb+ infinitive</span> in affirmative statements to express necessity for something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the following structure when writing a verb+ infinitive in affirmative statements with <strong>need to.</strong> </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><strong>Subject + Need + to + Basic form of a verb + Complement</strong></div></br></div> Example: </br><i> I <strong>need to</strong> design a model.</i></span></div> </br></br>Remember to add an <i>-s</i> to the verb <strong>need</strong> when used with third person singular nouns. The verb that comes after the preposition <i>to</i>, always keeps its basic form.   </br></br>Example: </br>  <i>She <strong>needs to</strong> learn about OOP."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to write a new software system for the company, but I don't know if it is a good idea to use OOP. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We need to consider that information so we can develop a new software model."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That is why, we need to create classes by object-oriented modeling the real world, so it can be easily understood."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reusability "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "use of existing components within the software, this is easier to do when they are categorized in classes."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, you can also get better reusability, this means you can categorize components in general classes.\u00a0"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "class "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "software design that describes generalities about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That is why, we need to create classes by object-oriented modeling the real world, so it can be easily understood."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inheritance "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "class or object you implement in the same way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, I need to review them, but I think these are: Abstraction, encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism.\u00a0"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "approach "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way you deal with something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: OOP is the best approach to writing a software."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "object-oriented modelling "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "process for developing a software with a OOP approach"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That is why, we need to create classes by object-oriented modeling the real world, so it can be easily understood."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "software model "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "software prototype"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to consider that information so we can develop a software model that tells us what the software must do and how it should work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose three benefits of using OOP."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Search more information about them. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a poster that explains those three benefits and promotes the use of OOP. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your poster with the rest of your class."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify benefits of OOP."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I look up about OOP benefits."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a poster to promote OOP. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my poster with the rest of the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Engineer</strong>:  I need to write a new software system for the company, but I don't know if it is a good idea to use OOP. </br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>:  OOP is the best approach to writing a software. Do you remember all those benefits of the OOP? </br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: Yes! These benefits are always around the ideas that are basic to OOP.</br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>: Do you know any of these ideas? </br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: Well, I need to review them, but I think these are: Abstraction, encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism. </br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>:  Are these ideas related to OOP principles? </br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: Well, these are also principles."}, {"time": "37000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Assistant</strong>:  What do you need to do with that information? </br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>:  We need to consider that information so we can develop a software model that tells us what the software must do and how it should work. </br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>:  Do we need to do this before creating our new software?</br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: Yes, we do. Remember that we are using fragile information, and when we create this new software, we need to make it comprehensible. </br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>: That is why, we need to create classes by object-oriented modeling the real world, so it can be easily understood."}, {"time": "68000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Assistant</strong>:  Can you tell me the specific benefits you get when using OOP to create a software?</br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: Well, the benefits are better maintainability, this means that the software can be more comprehensible and less fragile; and better abstraction, which means that you can model information and behavior together.</br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>: Do those benefits include things like good reusability? </br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: Well, you can also get better reusability, this means you can categorize components in general classes. </br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>: Great! So, let's start."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can list some benefits to use OOP. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can recall the ideas that are basic for OOP. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about things to consider before writing a software."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Think on any brand new software, what do you think are the advantages and disadvantages of that software?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think you need to create a new software?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Software in an Object-Oriented Way"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [2], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " An engineer needs to understand the benefits you get when using <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">OOP</span>."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"type": "tips", "content": [{"tip_id": 0, "type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> \u201cOOP\u201d </span> means Object Oriented Programming"}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "template_override": 1, "id": 1}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " The use of OOP brings important benefits. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Activity 1"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Select all the correct answers."}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have 2 attempts to submit you